OL,3,GNEWSANo biological males in women's
OL,4,Aprisons, Scottish Prison Service
OL,5,Aconfirms
OL,6,
OL,7,FAll transgender inmates have been moved
OL,8,Fout of women's prisons, according to
OL,9,Fthe Scottish Prison Service (SPS).
OL,11,FSPS deputy chief executive Adam Jobson
OL,12,Ftold Holyrood's Equalities Committee
OL,13,Fthat a small number of transgender
OL,14,Fprisoners had been moved. He said that
OL,15,Ftrans women - biological males who
OL,16,Fidentify as women - were now held in
OL,17,Fmen's prisons.
OL,19,FThe move was to comply with a judge's
OL,20,Fruling in June, that sex segregation in
OL,21,Fprisons must be based on biological sex
OL,22,Frather than gender identity.
OL,23,APub: 12-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,425,420,260,160,0,100
